{
  "clause_name": "SERVICES",
  "issue": "The clause lacks clarity and consistency in jurisdiction and venue provisions.",
  "suggested_language": "(a) This Agreement and any matters arising from or in connection with it shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New York, excluding its conflict of law principles. (b) The parties agree that any legal suit, action, or proceeding arising out of or related to the Professional Services shall be brought exclusively in the courts located in the Borough of Manhattan, City of New York, State of New York, or the United States District Court for the Southern District of New York. Each party irrevocably submits to the exclusive jurisdiction of such courts and waives any objection to the venue or inconvenience of the forum. (c) The submission to jurisdiction by any Provider does not limit the Provider's right to initiate proceedings in any other jurisdiction, nor does it preclude the initiation of proceedings in any other jurisdiction.",
  "rationale": "The revised language clarifies the exclusive jurisdiction and venue, reducing ambiguity and potential legal disputes over jurisdictional issues. It also ensures consistency by aligning the venue waiver with the exclusive jurisdiction agreement, thereby protecting the client from unexpected legal challenges in inconvenient forums."
}

