  "suggested_language": "2. Provider shall make commercially reasonable efforts to defend and represent all incoming Visa and MasterCard chargebacks on behalf of Company pursuant to the terms below. Provider will comply with all applicable Payment Network Regulations. 3. Company understands that to properly render the Chargeback Services, Company must provide Provider with timely access to necessary information as specified herein. Failure by Company to provide such access within [specified time frame] shall be considered a material breach of the Agreement. 4. If Provider is unable to successfully defend and represent a chargeback on behalf of Company, Provider will provide Company with the originating Payment Network chargeback advice and corresponding financial debit within [specified number of days] after original receipt of the chargeback advice and debit through the originating Payment Network. Company may request, within [specified number of days] of receiving the chargeback advice, the information Provider used in the initial defense of the filed chargeback. 5. Provider shall implement financial and managerial/billing reporting to support Chargeback Services. Reporting will be designed, implemented, and delivered in a mutually agreeable manner, with changes subject to mutual consent. 6. Company shall: (a) provide Provider with reasonable and monitored access to ticketing and other agreed internal administration systems necessary for Chargeback Services, with the possibility of altering or enhancing system access and processes by mutual agreement; (b) configure access rights for Provider's Chargeback Services team to Company's systems to permit chargeback resolution and representment processes; (c) ensure systems are consistently available to Provider employees and agents providing the Chargeback Services; and (d) ensure system access rights are defined to permit access to travel data for all card products (e.g., VISA and MasterCard) supported by the Chargeback Services.",
