{
  "clause_name": "LIABILITY",
  "issue": "The clause lacks clarity on the scope of liability exclusions and may not adequately protect against all potential liabilities.",
  "suggested_language": "10.3 Limitations of Liability: (a) The limitations of liability in this Clause 10.3 shall not exclude a Party\u2019s liability for Losses caused by that Party\u2019s gross negligence, willful misconduct, or fraud. (b) Komainu (or its Affiliates) shall not be liable for any reduction in the value of Assets, expressed in any currency or substitute value. (c) Komainu (or its Affiliates) shall not be liable for Losses due to events beyond its reasonable control. (d) Komainu (or its Affiliates) shall not be liable for indirect or consequential Losses, including loss of profits, contracts, revenue, opportunities, anticipated savings, business, or goodwill, even if foreseeable. (e) Komainu\u2019s liability for Theft is limited to the greater of the Service Fees for the 24 months preceding the Theft or the insurance proceeds received, prorated among affected clients. (f) Except for Theft, Komainu\u2019s liability shall not exceed the Service Fees for the 12 months preceding the event causing liability. 10.4 Alleviation: Komainu shall not be liable for non-compliance with obligations if acting on professional advice or required to comply with applicable law or regulation.",
  "rationale": "The revised language provides clearer boundaries for liability, ensuring that Komainu is not held accountable for unforeseeable or uncontrollable events, while still holding parties accountable for gross negligence or fraud. This protects the client by clearly delineating the scope of liability and ensuring that liability limits are enforceable and compliant with applicable laws."
}

{
  "clause_name": "TERMINATION",
  "issue": "The clause does not explicitly address the handling of disputes or the return of confidential information upon termination.",
  "suggested_language": "14.7 Accrued Rights: (a) Termination of this MSA or any Order Form, howsoever arising, shall be without prejudice to the rights, duties, and liabilities of the Parties accrued prior to termination. (b) Komainu shall be entitled to receive all Service Fees and other Sums Due accrued under this MSA or a terminating Order Form up to but excluding the date of termination thereof, howsoever that termination may have arisen. 14.8 Continued Effect: Provisions in this MSA or any Order Form which, expressly or impliedly, grant or give rise to continuing rights or impose or give rise to continuing obligations shall operate, survive and lawfully have effect after termination of this MSA or Order Form. 14.9 Dispute Resolution: Any disputes arising from or in connection with the termination of this MSA shall be resolved in accordance with the dispute resolution procedures set forth in Section 16. 14.10 Return of Confidential Information: Upon termination of this MSA, each Party shall promptly return or destroy all confidential information of the other Party in its possession, except as required to be retained by law or regulation.",
  "rationale": "Including provisions for dispute resolution and the return of confidential information ensures that both parties have a clear process for resolving any disagreements and protects sensitive information, thereby minimizing potential legal risks and safeguarding the client's interests."
}

{
  "clause_name": "DATA_PROTECTION",
  "issue": "The clause lacks specificity regarding the obligations and responsibilities of the parties involved in data protection and does not address the notification requirements for data breaches.",
  "suggested_language": "1. Data Protection Obligations: Each party shall comply with all applicable Data Protection Obligations, including but not limited to the UK GDPR, the Data Protection Act 2018, and any other applicable data protection laws. 2. Data Breach Notification: In the event of a Personal Data Breach, the Processor shall notify the Controller without undue delay and, where feasible, not later than 72 hours after becoming aware of the breach. The notification shall include, at a minimum, the nature of the breach, the categories and approximate number of data subjects and data records concerned, and the measures taken or proposed to be taken to address the breach. 3. Sub-Processor Obligations: The Processor shall ensure that any New Sub-Processor agrees in writing to comply with data protection obligations equivalent to those imposed on the Processor under this Agreement. The Processor shall remain fully liable for any breach of data protection obligations by the Sub-Processor. 4. Data Transfers: Any Restricted Transfer shall be conducted in compliance with Data Protection Obligations, utilizing Standard Contractual Clauses or other approved mechanisms to ensure lawful data transfers.",
  "rationale": "This change provides clear obligations and responsibilities for both parties, ensuring compliance with data protection laws. It also establishes a clear protocol for notifying the Controller of data breaches, which is crucial for timely response and mitigation. By specifying the obligations of Sub-Processors, the clause ensures that data protection responsibilities are maintained throughout the data processing chain, thereby protecting the client's interests."
}

