{
  "clause_name": "SERVICES",
  "issue": "The clause lacks clarity and specificity regarding the scope of implied services and the process for handling changes due to acquisitions.",
  "suggested_language": "4.1. Services (a) Obligation to Provide Services Starting on the Commencement Date of each Service Agreement and continuing throughout the Service Agreement Term, Provider shall provide the Services to Customer and to other members of the Customer Group designated by Customer. The Parties acknowledge and agree that there are functions, responsibilities, activities, and tasks not specifically described in the Agreement but are required for the proper performance and provision of the Services. These shall be deemed to be included within the scope of the Services if they are a necessary and customary part of the Customer Group\u2019s business or inherently part of any New Service. For Services under Service Agreement No. 1, this includes all services performed by Provider during the twelve (12) months prior to August 1, 2020, unless expressly changed in this Agreement or rendered obsolete by the Transformation Plan or service evolution. (b) Affiliate Participation (i) If Customer or any Affiliate of Customer merges with or acquires a Person or assets from a Third Party (an 'Acquired Business'), at Customer\u2019s election, such Acquired Business will become part of the Customer Group, and the Services shall be provided to the Acquired Business. The Charges will be adjusted according to the Agreement's terms and charging methodologies. If material changes in service volumes, delivery costs, or delivery methods arise from integrating the Acquired Business, not covered by the existing terms, the Parties will renegotiate all affected Charges in good faith per the Change Control Procedures. Integration charges for the Acquired Business will be handled on a Project basis, per the applicable Service Agreement's terms and pricing. If the Acquired Business is party to an agreement with Provider, and services under such agreement are integrated with the Services, any termination charges under such agreement shall be waived.",
  "rationale": "The revised language clarifies the scope of implied services and ensures that any changes due to acquisitions are handled transparently and fairly, protecting the client's interests by ensuring predictable service delivery and cost adjustments."
}

{
  "clause_name": "SERVICES",
  "issue": "The clause lacks specificity regarding timelines and responsibilities, which may lead to ambiguity in execution.",
  "suggested_language": "6.1. Disaster Recovery and Business Continuity Services (a) Disaster Recovery Services Provider shall deliver Disaster Recovery Services in accordance with the Service Agreement, ensuring compliance with all applicable Charges outlined therein. (b) Disaster Upon determination by Provider that a disaster or business disruption is imminent or has occurred, Provider shall notify Customer within one hour and immediately implement all actions and precautions as per the 'Disaster Recovery and Business Continuity Requirements' Schedule or the applicable disaster recovery or business continuity plan. Provider shall diligently pursue these actions to prevent or minimize service interruption. Provider will update Customer on the status of the disaster or business disruption at least every 12 hours. Upon resolution, Provider shall furnish Customer with a detailed incident report within 48 hours, outlining the cause and resolution actions taken.",
  "rationale": "This change introduces clear timelines for notifications and updates, ensuring that the Customer is promptly informed and can make timely decisions. It also specifies the requirement for a detailed incident report, which enhances accountability and transparency, protecting the client's interests."
}

{
  "clause_name": "SERVICES",
  "issue": "The clause lacks clarity on the handling of disputed charges and does not specify the currency for payments.",
  "suggested_language": "8.1. Charges: In consideration of the Services under each Service Agreement, Customer will pay Provider the Charges set forth in the 'Charges' Schedule to each Service Agreement, which will include the payments and payment-related terms. Except as expressly set forth in the Agreement, including the 'Charges' Schedule, to the applicable Service Agreement, no other amounts are payable under the Agreement. Undisputed Charges are due and payable 60 days after receipt of invoice from Provider. Disputed Charges must be notified to the Provider within 30 days of receipt of the invoice, with the undisputed portion payable as per the original terms. Customer\u2019s payment shall be made by wire transfer in [specify currency] to an account designated by Provider. Any unused credits against future payments (including Service Level Credits) owed to either Party by the other pursuant to a Service Agreement will be paid to the applicable Party within 60 days after the expiration or termination of the Service Agreement.",
  "rationale": "Adding a mechanism for handling disputed charges protects the client by ensuring they are not obligated to pay amounts they contest without resolution. Specifying the currency for payments avoids potential misunderstandings or disputes related to currency fluctuations or conversions."
}

